WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 line:92%
-I am a big fan of the show.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.902 line:92%
I'm so happy it's coming back.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would imagine this was
a very exciting role to get,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.540
yet you had some family members
who were not that excited

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were first cast.
-Me grandad wasn't very happy.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.179
Yeah, he's like, "Bloody hell,
you're not playing bloody Burke,

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
are you?"

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.849
He's from Nottingham,
which that probably doesn't make

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
much sense here.
But it's in the North

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
of England, or the middle
of England, yeah.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he called him a Burke?
-A Burke.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
Meaning?

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Meaning an idiot.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.591 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.460
-Because my granddad thinks that
Prince Phillip is an idiot.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he's not!
He's a very astute, clever,

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
charming, intelligent man,
I like to think.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
But so is my granddad.
He's, you know.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you -- you actually met
Prince William?

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.271 line:92%
-I met William and Harry, yes.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And had -- had
the show been on yet?

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:46.346
-I was -- I was presented
to William at the Polo.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.149
-Oh, that's the most British
thing that anyone's ever said

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this show.
-Yes, I know.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.585
But I was presented to William.
-That was like a hat trick --

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
presented,
Prince William, the polo.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.956 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm not really
very posh, either.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I talk posh
when I'm nervous.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, your -- your grandfather
says "Burke."

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
We know where you're from.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:08.268
And the lady next to me said,
"Oh, yeah, he's playing --"

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "Don't do it,
don't do it, don't do it,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't do it."
"He's playing --"

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, don't do it."
"He's playing Prince Phillip."

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went, "Oh,
Christ, she's done it."

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
And all he did was,
he went, "Legend."

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-I'm like, "What?"

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.549 line:92%
And he went, "He's a legend."

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went, "Yeah,
he is a legend."

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, that's great.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.387
It's very nice to hear
that from Prince William.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.689
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Now this is an interesting time

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the show.
It's going to keep going,

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you will --
both you and Claire

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.028 size:84% position:42%
are going to be recast.
-We've been moved on.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause they're going
to get older actors

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play them older.
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.035 size:81% position:41%
-Are you -- it has not
been cast yet, right?

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that correct?
-Well, I don't know.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you maybe know.
-I maybe know.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.240 line:92%
I mean I don't know if I know.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not meant to know,
but I maybe know.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, now, is part of you
though, "Oh, that's who

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
they think I'm going to look
like in ten years?"

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If it's the person
that it could be,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.784 line:92%
I was just totally flattered.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, great.
-How marvellous.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.221 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Oh, that's exciting.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you --
This has happened once before.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.125
We were talking backstage,
one of my favorite movies is

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
"In Bruges."
-Yes.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You played --
There was a flashback scene

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you played
a young Ralph Fiennes.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes.
-Which is a fan --

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.432
I mean, that is -- you can't ask
for more than that.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.701
-And it's Martin McDonagh,
and it's such a great film.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Ralph is one of
my favorite actors.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:19.906
I just think he's electric, so.
-So, is this on the level of --

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.875
Is this Ralph good, or is
this maybe a little lower?

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, where are you at here?
-Well, you know --

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I don't want to
kind of speculate too much.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
But yeah, no, he's brilliant.
-Okay, good.

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If it's the person
I think it might be.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's incredibly
handsome as well.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:32.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which, you know --
-All right, good.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, fingers crossed for you.
I really hope.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:38.825
-I have morphed into someone
far better looking than I.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.226
-I want to ask about this,
because obviously when you

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.996
take on something like playing a
member of the the royal family,

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:46.466
there's going to be intense,
sort of, fan attention to it.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:49.235
But you maybe did something that
has even more fan attention

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you played
the eleventh doctor...

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...on "Doctor Who."

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.175 size:75% position:38%
-When I played Harry
in "In Bruges," yes.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.075 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, when you got that role
to play the doctor, had you --

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you understand that world
you were stepping into?

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not really.
Nothing -- nothing can really

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
prepare you for the sort of
enormity of that part.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
And funny enough, one of
the papers sort of found out

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:14.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then -- at the time,
I had a Brazilian girlfriend.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:18.031 size:81% position:41%
And one of the British
newspapers went up to

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:18.831 line:92%
my granddad's house, again.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.500
I'm just bringing my poor
granddad into it again.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.736
And they knocked on his door and
they said, "Oh, you know,"

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they actually offered him
a huge amount of money,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said,
"Who's his girlfriend?"

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "I don't
bloody know, Carmen Miranda."

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.481
Who's a famous Brazilian singer.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And slammed the door
in their face.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went, "Yes, Gramps.
Good lad."

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:42.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.923 line:92%
-But the fans, were they great?

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.859
Like, once you enter that world.
-Yes, I mean, at first

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:50.063
they hated me because David was
so popular and they were like,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't break 'Doctor Who.'"
And everyone hated me

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.700 size:88% position:44%
and I thought, "Oh, God,
I'm just going to die."

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.369
And it was an awful thing.
But then eventually, I hope,

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.503 line:92%
that they've now accepted me.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you know, the great thing
about that show is,

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.543 size:84% position:42%
is that they love or
they hate their doctor.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.644 line:92%
So everyone has their doctor.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.914
And for some people, I will be
their doctor and to some people,

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
David Tennant will be theirs,
and et cetera, et cetera.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's a nice way
of looking at it.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.987
You -- Again, we've heard a lot
about your grandfather

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I'm very happy about.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:18.324
He's a top boy.
-And so, seems like a salty guy.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
You seem again, very kind,
very well put together.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:23.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
Certainly, we see you
on that show.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.264
Me?
-Yeah, very polite, but then --

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:28.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you very much.
-True story that you were --

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:31.170 size:78% position:39%
a fight? Did you get
in fights in schools?

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.172 size:75% position:38%
-Oh, yes, I have had
a fight at school.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just one though?
-Well, yeah.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:36.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Well -- well, yeah.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:39.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
One that was significant,
I suppose.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Memorable?
-Yeah, you know.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:42.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ish.
-Did you start it?

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
What happened?
-No, I didn't start it,

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually.
It was in history,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:50.189
and that was the one subject
that I was in the top set for.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm more intelligent
than I look.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know,
we were debating a point,

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was one
very clever lad, chap,

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:05.371
in school, who was demeaning me,
frankly, and my point of view.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then, you know,
I proceeded --

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.076 line:92%
Anyway, I mean, you know --

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.713
I leapt over the desk and told
him I would shove his trumpet

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
up his ass.

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:18.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause he was
the school trumpeter.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.120 line:92%
-And he was a smug pillock.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.157 line:92%
-That escalated so quickly.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:27.260
-Yeah, and then there was
fisticuffs, and I got suspended

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I went home and I told
my dad and he laughed.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.898
-Okay.
-And I thought I had him on side

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
and tnen I was very nonchalant
about it.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my dad was like,
"Oy, reign it in.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sort it out,
don't get suspended."

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:41.107
-Well, I think if anything,
he should have given that speech

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:43.643
to his father, because obviously
that's where it all started.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:44.610 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah exactly.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.080
-Well, hey, man, thanks so much
for being here.

